From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:44:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Thief: an unchanged object keeps its BLAS

Each moving object of some size has a BLAS of its own (objectBlas), refitted
every frame from the frame before's. Most of them are not moving: a statue,
a crate, a tree kept out of view for its shadow come the same frame after
frame, and over a hundred refits a frame were most of the 2 ms the graphics
card spent on 'Build dynamic BLAS' in Reflections in Red. An object whose
geometry is the same as last frame (its content keys) now keeps the BLAS it
had: nothing is encoded for it. The BLAS a frame uses is the slot last
written; a changed object is written into a slot no frame in flight reads,
refitted from the one before. Unchanged for 30 frames after a refit or a
fast build, it is built once more for tracing. RTGL1_METAL_NO_OBJECT_KEEP=1:
refitted each frame, as before. The stats line counts them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0137FfF2kXgpYFjmGxKqakLV
